You are debugging a production issue where high-throughput migration to Java 21 Virtual Threads (`Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()`) caused severe throughput degradation and thread starvation under heavy load. Profiling reveals that carrier platform threads are stuck in `TIMED_WAITING` or `BLOCKED` states.

java
@Component
public class RemoteDataFetcher {
    private final Map<String, String> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public String getData(String key) {
        return cache.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> fetchFromExternalApi(k));
    }

    private synchronized String fetchFromExternalApi(String key) {
        // Blocking I/O over HTTP
        return restTemplate.getForObject("https://api.internal/data/" + key, String.class);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where database records updated asynchronously inside a Spring application are missing changes. The method is annotated with Spring's `@Transactional`, but operations chained inside `CompletableFuture` do not roll back on error and fail to persist database changes reliably.

java
@Service
public class OrderProcessingService {
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public CompletableFuture<Void> processOrderAsync(Order order) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            order.setStatus("PROCESSING");
            return orderRepository.save(order);
        }).thenAcceptAsync(savedOrder -> {
            // External RPC service call
            paymentGateway.charge(savedOrder);
            savedOrder.setStatus("COMPLETED");
            orderRepository.save(savedOrder);
        });
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an aggregator service calling 15 downstream services via `CompletableFuture.allOf()` experiences severe memory growth and lingering socket connections whenever a single downstream service fails with a timeout exception.

java
List<CompletableFuture<Response>> futures = services.stream()
    .map(service -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> service.callRemoteEndpoint()))
    .toList();

CompletableFuture<Void> allFutures = CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0]));

try {
    allFutures.join();
} catch (Exception e) {
    log.error("Aggregation failed", e);
    throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
}
